<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ricciarda Malaspina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1497–1553</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ricciarda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaspina">Malaspina</a> (1497–1553) was Marchioness of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massa-tuscany">Massa</a> and Lady of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a>, heiress of the Malaspina lords of Massa. Her marriage in 1520 to Lorenzo Cybo, a nephew of Pope Leo X, brought the state to the Cybo family, and she governed it herself for long periods. Their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberico-i-cybo-malaspina">Alberico I Cybo-Malaspina</a> was made Prince of Massa in 1568.</p></div>
